                <pb facs="0234" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1177: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-20T19:00:00-04:00">June 20, 1930—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>204. Your 451, June 17, 1 p.m., last sentence.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d124-f1"/>
                    The Department assumes that the Legation has at all times in mind possible
                    necessity for the issuing of instructions to consular officers in China or for
                    requesting the despatch of naval vessels with a view to providing for the safety
                    and well-being of American consular officials and other American citizens.
                    Please keep the Department fully informed in this regard.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
